              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesPhenomenology"} Phenomenology
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+reduction"} Kaluza-Klein reduction
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82+manifolds"} G₂ manifolds
            (notably
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freund-Rubin+compactifications"} Freund-Rubin compactifications
            and variants) yields an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-dimensional+supergravity"} 4-dimensional supergravity
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            (arising from the KK-modes of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            (arising from the KK-models of the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            as the analog of the KK-compactification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} Calabi-Yau manifolds
            (see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+CY4-manifolds"} F-theory on CY4-manifolds
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
                of higher dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                with minimal (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                ) supersymmetry
              \:
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th perspective
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
                    with
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+CY4-manifolds"} F-theory on CY4-manifolds
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory+on+CY3-manifolds"} heterotic string theory on CY3-manifolds
          %p
            In order for this to yield
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenologically
            interesting effective physics the compactification space must be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-orbifold"} G₂-orbifold
            (hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+orbifold"} Riemannian orbifold
            of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+holonomy"} special holonomy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+groups"} stabilizer groups
            will encode the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"} nonabelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            of the effective theory by “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+quantum+field+theory"}> geometric engineering of quantum field theory
            ” (
            %a{:href => "#Acharya98"}> Acharya 98
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah-Witten 01, section 6
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EnhancedGaugeGroups"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            obtaining or approximating the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            by this procedure see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
          %h2#G2Manifolds Details
          %h3#VacuumSolutionsAndTorsion Vacuum solutions
          %p
            Genuine
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-manifold"} G₂-manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            fibers, these having vanishing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ricci+curvature"} Ricci curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            solutions of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Acharya02"} Acharya 02, p. 9
            = succeed "-field" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-holonomy\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#TheCField"} below
          %p
            Notice that vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            (i.e.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+derivative"} covariant derivative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+a+Cartan+connection"} torsion
            of the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            is in each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
            the canonical torsion of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+torsion+constraint"} torsion constraint
            already just for the bosonic part
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E^a)
            of the super-vielbein
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E^a, E^\alpha)
            implies (together with the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of supergravity, hence here the vacuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
            in the 11d
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %h3#ComplexifiedModuli Complexified moduli space
          %p
            For vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau \coloneqq C_3 + i \phi_3
          %p
            of the (flat) supergravity
            = succeed "-field" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_3
            and the 3-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_3
            of the
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic coordinate
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of a
            = succeed "-manifold," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HarveyMoore99"} Harvey-Moore 99, (2.7)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Acharya02"} Acharya 02, (32) (59) (74)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GrigorianYau08"} Grigorian-Yau 08, (4.57)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AcharyaBobkov08"} Acharya-Bobkov 08, (4)
          %p
            Notice that restricted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+submanifolds"} associative submanifolds
            this combination becomes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 3
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %mi vol
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_3 + i vol
            = succeed "-contributions" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+instanton"} membrane instanton
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+volume"} complex volume
          %h3#EnhancedGaugeGroups Nonabelian gauge groups and chiral fermions at orbifold singularities
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of vacuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            on a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-manifold"} G₂-manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            results in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D1+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=1 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)^{b_2(Y)}
            and with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_3(Y)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+scalar+fields"} complex scalar fields
            which are neutral (not charged) under this gauge group (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_\bullet(Y)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Betti+numbers"} Betti numbers
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Acharya02"} Acharya 02, section 2.3
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
          %p
            But when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            then:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                at an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularity"} ADE singularity
                there is
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+gauge+symmetry"} enhanced gauge symmetry
                in that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
                (which a priori is copies of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                of the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"} nonabelian
                (
                %a{:href => "#Acharya98"}> Acharya 98
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#Acharya00"} Acharya 00
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#Acharya02"} Acharya 02, section 3
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#BBS07"} BBS 07, p. 422, 436
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "string+phenomenology#IbanezUranga12"} Ibáñez-Uranga 12, section 6.3.3
                %a{:href => "string+phenomenology#Wijnholt14"} Wijnholt 14, part III
                (from which the graphics below is grabbed));
            %li
              %p
                at a (non-orbifold)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+singularity"} conical singularity
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+fermions"} chiral fermions
                appear (
                %a{:href => "#Witten01"}> Witten 01, p. 3
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah-Witten 01
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#AcharyaWitten01"} Acharya-Witten 01
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#BerglundBrandhuber02"} Berglund-Brandhuber 02
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#BourjailyEspahbodi08"} Bourjaily-Espahbodi 08
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+singularity"} conical singularity
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+fermions"} chiral fermions
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+singularities"} conical singularities
            are supposed/assumed to be isolated (
            %a{:href => "#Witten01"}> Witten 01, section 2
            ), while the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularities"} ADE singularities
            are supposed/assumed to be of
            = succeed "-4" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten01"} Witten 01, section 3
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Barrett06"} Barrett 06
          %p In the absence of a proper microscopic definition of M-theory, the first point is argued indirectly in at least these ways:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The fact that under
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
                to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
                the singularity becomes special points of intersecting
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
                for which the gauge enhancement is folklore (
                %a{:href => "#Sen97"}> Sen 97
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#Witten01"} Witten 01, p. 1
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#CveticShiuUranga01"} Cvetic-Shiu-Uranga 01
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality
                between M-theory compactified on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
                on a 3-torus (
                %a{:href => "#AcharyaWitten01"}> Acharya-Witten 01
                ). Here it is fairly well understood that at the degeneration points of the K3-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
                enhanced nonabelian gauge symmetry appears (e.g.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#AcharyaGukov04"} Acharya-Gukov 04, section 5.1
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "ALE+space#IntriligatorSeiberg96"} Intriligator-Seiberg 96
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularity"} ADE singularity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2/\Gamma
                generically constitutes a point in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
                in the
                %a{:href => "N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory#ModuliSpacesOfVacua"} Higgs branch
                of a super Yang-Mills theory.
            %li#Blowup
              %div{:style => "float:left;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
                %img{:alt => "ADE 2Cycle", :src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ADESingularity.jpg", :width => "600"}/
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/blow-up"} blow-up
                of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
                happens to be a union of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spheres"} 2-spheres
                touching pairwise in one point, such as to form the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagram
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+group"} simple Lie group
                which under the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
                corresponds to the given
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
                isotropy group.
              %p
                (graphics grabbed from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+homotopy+and+super+M-branes"} HSS18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
                may
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrap
                these 2-cycles and since before blow-up they are of vanishing size, this corresponds to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
                under which the M2-branes become
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                stretching between coincident
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
                located on the D-branes, and hence these same nonabelian degrees of freedom have had to be present already at the level of the M2-branes. This is due to (
                %a{:href => "#Sen97"}> Sen 97
                ), for more see at
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
            %li
              %p
                In the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                description the ADE singularity maps to the locus where the F-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
                degenerates with 2-cycles in the elliptic fibers shrinking to 0. Via
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
                this manifestly takes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapping
                these elliptic fibers to an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
                stretching between
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)
                gauge symmetry by the usual string theory argument about
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
          %p
            Also notice that at least the
            = succeed "-enhancement" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            at
            = succeed "-singularities" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_k
            = succeed "-enhancement" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory of
            = succeed "-coincident" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            sitting at the orbifold singularity: this is the statement of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ABJM+model"} ABJM model
          %h3#TheCField
            Solutions with non-vanishing
            = succeed "-field" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p#FluxBreaksSuSy
            %strong Claim:
            %em
              There is no warped
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
              of M-theory on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_4 \times F_7
              which retains at least
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
              in 4d while at the same time having non-vanishing
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
              of the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#AcharyaSpence00"}> Acharya-Spence 00
            ) see the Introduction of (
            %a{:href => "#BeasleyWitten02"}> Beasley-Witten 02
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            In compactifications with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+G%E2%82%82+holonomy"} weak G₂ holonomy
            it is the defining 4-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_4
            (the one which for strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82+manifolds"} G₂ manifolds
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge dual
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#BilalDerendingerSfetos"} Bilal-Serendinger-Sfetos 02, section 6
          %p
            Consider a
            = succeed "-Ansatz" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 11
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{11} = (X_4,g_4) \times (X_7,g_7)
            and
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 4
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mi vol
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_4 = f vol_{X_4}
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 7
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %msubsup
                        %mi e
                        %mn 7
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_7 = \tilde g e_7^\ast \phi_4
          %p
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_7
            are given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            fields on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_4
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_7
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_4
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge dual
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            give
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 4
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 3
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 7
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 2
                    %mo )
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R_4 = - \frac{1}{3}\left(f^2 + \frac{7}{2} \tilde g^2\right) g_4
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 7
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mn 5
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 2
                    %mo )
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R_7 = \frac{1}{6}\left(f^2 + 5 \tilde g^2\right) g_7
          %p
            (where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_7
            is the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} metric tensor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifolds"} Einstein manifolds
            (
            %a{:href => "#BilalDerendingerSfetos"}> BSS 02, (5.4)
            ). The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi d
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo −
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde g\left(
                  d \phi - f \star\phi
                  \\right)
                  \= 0
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi e
                    %mn 7
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi = e_7^\ast \phi_3
            the pullback of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
            (
            %a{:href => "#BilalDerendingerSfetos"}> BSS 02, (5.5)
            ), saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∝
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \propto \star F_7
            exhibits
            %a{:href => "G2+manifold#WeakG2Holonomy"} weak G₂-holonomy
            with weakness parameter given by the component of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_4
          %h3#Confinement Confinement?
          %p
            An idea for a strategy towards a proof of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D1+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=1 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            via two different but conjecturally equivalent realizations as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            has been given in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah-Witten 01, section 6
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AcharyaGukov04"} Acharya-Gukov 04, section 5.3
          %p
            The idea here is to consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} G₂-manifolds
            that locally around a special point are of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Cone
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %mtext or
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Cone
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_{1,\Gamma}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\big( S^3 / \Gamma \big) \times Cone\big(S^3\big)
                  \\phantom{AA}
                  \\text{or}
                  \\phantom{AA}
                  X_{2,\Gamma}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  S^3 \times Cone\big(S^3/\Gamma\big)
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
                that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
                canonically by left-multiplication on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ≃
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \simeq
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cone(\cdots)
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+cone"} metric cone
                construction.
          %p
            This means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{1,\Gamma}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{2,\Gamma}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is not the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \neq 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            with an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularity"} ADE singularity
          %p
            Now the lore of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            predicts that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{1,\Gamma}
                yields a 4d theory without massless fields (since there are no massless modes on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{1,\Gamma}
            %li
              %p
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{2,\Gamma}
                yields
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
                in 4d coupled to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+fermions"} chiral fermions
          %p
            both of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dual
            by thinking of them in two different ways as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on the 8-manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HP%5E2"} HP^2
            (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"}> Atiyah-Witten 01, p. 75 onwards
            ).
          %p
            So in the first case a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap"} mass gap
            is manifest, while non-abelian gauge theory is not visible, while in the second case it is the other way around.
          %p
            But if there were an argument that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            is in fact equivalent for compactification both on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{1,\Gamma}
            and on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{2,\Gamma}
          %p
            This approach is suggested in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah-Witten 01, pages 84-85
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahMaldacenaVafa00"} Atiyah-Maldacena-Vafa 00
